# jemdoc: showsource
= Yaqi Xie

~~~
{}{img_left}{Resources/YaqiXie_photo_202610.JPG}{Yaqi Xie}{180}{270}
I am a fifth-year PhD student in Operations Management at Booth School of Business, University of Chicago.
I am very fortunate to be co-advised by Prof. [https://xin.engineering.cornell.edu/ Linwei Xin]
and Prof. [https://willma353.github.io/ Will Ma].
Previously, I received a B.S. in Mathematics and Applied Mathematics from Zhejiang University.\n


My research develops scalable learning and optimization methods for operational decision-making,
with applications in supply chain management and resource allocation.
Combining theoretical analysis with practical deployment, I study how operational structure can improve AI methods at scale,
how to learn effectively over long horizons, and when simple models and policies are sufficient.
As data and operations grow in scale, I am excited to explore how AI reshapes operational systems
and how we can guide its application to operational problems while preserving interpretability and providing managerial insights.\n



*I am on the 2026-2027 academic job market!*

Email: yaqi.xie@chicagobooth.edu\n

